🚀 Week 3 – Day 2 StringBuffer, StringBuilder & Regular Expressions ☕

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

When working with text in Java, you often need to:

✔ Modify strings efficiently
✔ Validate patterns such as emails, phone numbers, and passwords

Java provides:

* `StringBuffer`
* `StringBuilder`
* Regular Expressions (Regex)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔄 1. Why Not Modify String Directly?

Strings are immutable.

```java id="intro1"
String str = "Java";
str = str + " Programming";
```

👉 A new object is created each time.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚡ 2. StringBuffer

`StringBuffer` is a mutable sequence of characters.

✔ Can modify text without creating new objects
✔ Thread-safe (synchronized)

---

📌 Example

```java id="sb1"
StringBuffer sb = new StringBuffer("Java");
sb.append(" Programming");
System.out.println(sb);
```

Output:

```text id="sb2"
Java Programming
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🚀 3. StringBuilder

`StringBuilder` is similar to `StringBuffer`, but faster.

✔ Mutable
✔ Not thread-safe
✔ Better performance in single-threaded applications

---

📌 Example

```java id="sb3"
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Hello");
sb.append(" World");
System.out.println(sb);
```

---

📊 String vs StringBuffer vs StringBuilder

| Feature     | String | StringBuffer | StringBuilder |
| ----------- | ------ | ------------ | ------------- |
| Mutable     | ❌ No   | ✔ Yes        | ✔ Yes         |
| Thread-safe | ✔ Yes  | ✔ Yes        | ❌ No          |
| Performance | Slow   | Medium       | Fast          |

